> (press! "RET")
! buffers:replace!: An occur line takes no line break
; A source line changed since the listing refuses the edit, so no
; change in the source is lost and no edit lands in the wrong place.
> (buffers:replace! b 4 4 "!")
> (views:set-point! (view) (+ (find-text (occur-buffer) "one foo") 7))
> (press! "Y")
> (list (source) (last-message))
#<edit 3>
! buffers:replace!: The source line changed; g lists it again
("one! foo\ntwo\nfoo three foo\nfour\n" "Undo")
; A change at the line's start stays before the line's anchor, so the
; line from it still reads as listed, and the edit lands in place.
> (buffers:replace! b 4 5 "")
> (buffers:replace! b 1 1 ">> ")
> (press! "Y")
> (source)
> (buffers:replace! b 1 4 "")
> (press! "Y")
> (source)
