"one fooYY\ntwo\nfoo three foo\nfour\n"
; A source that refuses the edit leaves *Occur*'s edit and says so.
> (buffers:define-layer locked (read-only))
> (buffers:add-span! (buffers:layer b locked) 1 (- (document:length (buffers:document b)) 1) 'locked)
> (views:set-point! (view) (+ (find-text (occur-buffer) "one fooY") 8))
> (press! "W")
> (list (listed) (source) (last-message))
> (buffers:remove-span! (buffers:layer b locked) 'locked)
("3 matches in 2 lines for \"foo\" in buffer: src\none fooYWY\ntwo\nfoo three foo\nfour\n" "one fooYY\ntwo\nfoo three foo\nfour\n" "Buffer ‘src’ is read only.")
